.TH "GLESHA-HISTORY" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-history \- list the snapshots of a set
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha history\fR SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the completed snapshots of SET, newest first, with their type, size, and remote copies.
.PP
If the catalog is encrypted and not yet open on this computer, it is downloaded and the catalog passphrase is requested.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Query the remotes for archive availability.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha history docs
glesha history docs \-\-refresh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-browse (1),
.BR glesha\-restore (1)
